the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    Härtefall anerkennen holds for *a case*.
    Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for *a case*.
    the answer to Einkommensgrenze unterschritten for *a case* is *a truth value*; scenario element.
    Einkommensgrenze unterschritten would hold for *a case*; unknown.

the knowledge base r4_11_context_pool includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/context-pool.ruml".

bgh 2024 is published at "https://www.bundesgerichtshof.de/2024/123".

bmf income tax is published at "https://www.bundesfinanzministerium.de/bmf-schreiben/2024-01-01-einkommensteuer".

estg 32a is published at "https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/estg/__32a.html".

guidelines is published at "https://www.example.gov/haertefall-richtlinien.pdf".

Härtefall anerkennen holds for a case if
    Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for the case.

Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for a case if
    the answer to Einkommensgrenze unterschritten for the case is true.

% Until a person answers, RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the answer to Einkommensgrenze unterschritten for the case is a truth value
    and Einkommensgrenze unterschritten would hold for the case.

scenario generated_1 is, as stated in "context-pool.ruml" at generated_1:
    % no data
    node_1 expects answers ["Härtefall anerkennen holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Härtefall anerkennen holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    node_2 expects answers ["Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_2 expects answers ["it is not the case that Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.

scenario generated_2 is, as stated in "context-pool.ruml" at generated_2:
    % every leaf answered yes
    the answer to Einkommensgrenze unterschritten for case 1 is true.
    node_1 expects answers ["Härtefall anerkennen holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_1 expects answers [].
    node_2 expects answers ["Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_2 expects answers [].

scenario generated_3 is, as stated in "context-pool.ruml" at generated_3:
    % the leaf 2 answered no, the others yes
    the answer to Einkommensgrenze unterschritten for case 1 is false.
    node_1 expects answers [].
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Härtefall anerkennen holds for case 1"].
    node_2 expects answers [].
    not_node_2 expects answers ["it is not the case that Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for case 1"].

scenario generated_4 is, as stated in "context-pool.ruml" at generated_4:
    % every leaf answered no
    the answer to Einkommensgrenze unterschritten for case 1 is false.
    node_1 expects answers [].
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Härtefall anerkennen holds for case 1"].
    node_2 expects answers [].
    not_node_2 expects answers ["it is not the case that Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for case 1"].

query node_1 is:
    Härtefall anerkennen holds for case 1.

query not_node_1 is:
    it is not the case that Härtefall anerkennen holds for case 1.

query node_2 is:
    Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for case 1.

query not_node_2 is:
    it is not the case that Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for case 1.

